A||||14||fotofrank||ACCEL 300 +
Z||000000||fotofrank||06-04-99||12:04 PM||||Anyone have experiance with the ACELL 300 + universal ingnition with matching coil? Would it be worth to put on an iron duke?
Z||000001||FieroMike||06-04-99||12:21 PM||||Frank,<br>I haven't had experience with the 4, but with the 6 I found that the ACCELL is more expensive and less productive as the MSD ignition.  Also MSD makes a specific module for the Fiero and a HO coil that fits in the stock location instead of mounted on the trunk.
Z||000002||theogre||06-04-99||12:54 PM||||I'd tend to use MSD since they make plug and play harnes parts as well. I don't like any system that requires choping wires. Splicing things together all to often results in hard to find problems down the road. ((Usually when you're way down the road in the midle of a monsoon.))<p>I think Moroso has some plug and play stuff too. Haven't looked in a while.... no one makes anything to improve the DIS rig,,, not even better coils but then DIS is pretty hot as it is.
Z||000003||Harry||06-04-99||04:19 PM||||FieroMike,<br>Could you send me the part numbers for the MSD ? I know my tired old 2.8 could benefit from some extra juice.
Z||000004||FieroMike||06-04-99||06:04 PM||||The part number for the GM Blaster SS Coil, is PN 8207, took mine 2 days to get in.  As far as the module, you will have to do your homework on www.msdignition.com  I threw away the box.  Sorry.  The module is $170.00 because the firing order is 1-2-3-4-5-6!  Normal v-6's only run $130.
Z||000005||ezsurf||06-04-99||07:48 PM||||FieroMike,<br>Do you have to replace the module with the coil if you use an MSD coil, or can you simply replace  stock coil with the one from MSD? (when using stock ignition)
Z||000006||FieroMike||06-05-99||11:24 AM||||ezsurf,<br>Yes, you can just change out the coil, and I would highly recommend it.  My car loves 4,000+ RPM with the new coil, it zips right through the band.  The GM coil likes to poop out in the higher RPM's.   Changing the module though will make a HUGE difference.
Z||000007||mwbackus||06-11-99||03:27 PM||||Hi,<br>   I just joined since I find alot of very useful info here.  I have a question concerning the reference to "module" made in this thread.  Does this refer to the ignition module foung in the distributor, or to the MSD box (ie.. 6AL)?  I am considering a 6AL and was not aware that a special version for the fireing order was needed, I hope not. :0  <br>
Z||000008||FieroMike||06-11-99||05:46 PM||||mwbackus,<br>The answer to the first question is yes, the module is at the base of the distributer.  This is bypassed with the new MSD module and it does have a special firing order of 1-2-3-4-5-6 instead of the typical v-6 firing order.  The module at the base of the distributer is dead weight when you are done!  Good luck!<br>Mike
Z||000009||theogre||06-11-99||07:32 PM||||I find that interesting myself..... Firing order is determined by plug wire location on the dist cap, and the wiring of the dist cap. Fiero uses a queer dist cap layout to give it the aparrent firing order of 123456, but really it's something else.... (I don't have the cap's internal plan handy.)<p>The dist module, and MSD unit, shouldn't care. Why they seem to I really don't know.
Z||000010||lowCG||06-11-99||10:21 PM||||I think the MSD coil has different requirements for dwell time than the factory coil,requiring a different processor(module),probably doesn't have anything to do with the(strange)firing order since that's downstream anyways.We don't set the dwell anymore with inductive triggering,but it still must be done,in the module.
Z||000011||mwbackus||06-12-99||01:11 PM||||Well, I am still a bit lost on this one.  What I conclude so far is that if one was to use the Part No. 8226 Blaster GM Coil they should also use EITHER a different module from MSD (ie.. Part No. 8364) OR an MSD Ignition box such as the 6AL.  I hope my assumptions are correct since I plan to use the Blaster GM Coil and the 6AL.  I have heard, from those that have done this, that a significant increase in higher rpm performance can result.
Z||000012||lowCG||06-12-99||01:23 PM||||I would ask MSD just what the difference is between having the 6AL box,or the replacement module.Probably better off with the 6AL,since that's what the company was founded on-Multiple Spark Discharge.
Z||000013||fotofrank||06-12-99||07:46 PM||||E-mailed MSD about my '84 iron duke. Thay reccomend an MSD6A p/n 6200 and MSD Blaster coil p/n 8226.The 6AL I belive has a built-in rev limiter.
